assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Budget Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The UA Little Rock Bowen School of Law is seeking an Adjunct Lecturer to teach during the Fall 2026 semester. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Juris Doctorate Degree from an accredited law school. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare for and teach the assigned course. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries; Ability to respond to the needs of students from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment; Ability to deliver course instruction and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles; Ability to use technology effectively in teaching; Ability to communicate effectively; Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and Additional Information: The Adjuncts need to be able to teach one of the following courses: Adv. Appellate Advocacy Lawyering Skills Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jennifer Jones, Assistant Finance Director, jljones27@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financi